WEBVTT

00:00:06.850 --> 00:00:09.110
Welcome back, Misaki.

00:00:12.990 --> 00:00:17.150
Come on now, Misaki. Throw me a bone here.

00:00:17.150 --> 00:00:18.220
What?

00:00:18.780 --> 00:00:20.700
Look at this!

00:00:20.700 --> 00:00:23.160
It's a Standing Fight Table 
(Name Subject to Change).

00:00:23.160 --> 00:00:24.680
Cool, don't you think?

00:00:24.680 --> 00:00:27.750
It was tough setting it up <i>all by myself.</i>

00:00:28.110 --> 00:00:30.460
Isn't it just a table with no chairs?

00:00:30.860 --> 00:00:32.450
I guess that's one way to put it...

00:00:32.810 --> 00:00:40.610
But this table, you see... It's a magic table that 
speeds up cardfights and makes them more thrilling!

00:00:40.610 --> 00:00:42.190
Ooh, cool!

00:00:42.190 --> 00:00:43.910
You changed the place up a bit!

00:00:43.910 --> 00:00:46.570
Then, the first to have a cardfight 
on that table will be...

00:00:46.570 --> 00:00:47.680
Me!

00:00:47.680 --> 00:00:50.380
Yes, Kamui the Great is 
always the top batter!

00:00:50.380 --> 00:00:51.730
YK, yo!

00:00:51.730 --> 00:00:54.660
Wait! Hold it, you guys!

00:00:54.660 --> 00:00:55.910
Welcome!

00:00:55.910 --> 00:00:57.460
Who're you callin' "you guys?"

00:00:57.460 --> 00:00:58.480
So there, so there!

00:00:58.480 --> 00:00:59.880
SS, yo!

00:00:59.880 --> 00:01:02.040
SS my S, you little...

00:01:02.040 --> 00:01:02.750
Hey!

00:01:02.750 --> 00:01:04.770
Oh, perfect timing.

00:01:04.770 --> 00:01:07.830
The first cardfight on my 
new table will be between

00:01:07.830 --> 00:01:12.170
Katsumi Morikawa and Kamui 
Katsuragi, if you please!

00:01:12.170 --> 00:01:15.900
What a wonderful way to 
inaugurate the new table!

00:01:19.030 --> 00:01:21.660
Sure! I, the Great Kamui, 
will be your opponent!

00:01:21.660 --> 00:01:23.020
Be grateful for that!

00:01:23.020 --> 00:01:25.900
Shut it! That's my line, buddy!

00:01:26.450 --> 00:01:28.780
Stand up! Vanguard!

00:02:59.350 --> 00:03:01.540
Attack, Asura Kaiser!

00:03:01.540 --> 00:03:03.200
Finish Hold!

00:03:05.260 --> 00:03:07.820
He lost to a damn grade-schooler again...

00:03:07.820 --> 00:03:10.850
Damn it! It's because I was 
facing the wrong direction!

00:03:10.850 --> 00:03:14.450
I dunno what to say... I 
won and I still feel bad...

00:03:14.450 --> 00:03:17.330
That's our Kamui the Great with 
his Record of Repeat Wins!

00:03:17.330 --> 00:03:18.660
RR, yo!

00:03:18.660 --> 00:03:20.020
Oh, cut it out.

00:03:20.020 --> 00:03:24.430
If I count this guy, my great record 
of repeat wins will be tainted!

00:03:24.430 --> 00:03:25.980
What did you say?!

00:03:25.980 --> 00:03:29.770
You don't like it, try 
winning next time, Lose-umi!

00:03:29.770 --> 00:03:31.310
My name is Katsumi!

00:03:31.310 --> 00:03:33.480
Katsumi Morikawa, damn you!

00:03:33.480 --> 00:03:34.880
Keep quiet!

00:03:34.880 --> 00:03:38.400
If you want to make a scene, do it outside 
so it doesn't bother the other customers!

00:03:41.150 --> 00:03:43.100
W-We're sorry...

00:03:43.100 --> 00:03:47.630
Now, now... You're also 
very important customers.

00:03:47.630 --> 00:03:49.170
For Pete's sake...

00:03:52.030 --> 00:03:54.420
Kai isn't coming today, is he?

00:03:54.420 --> 00:03:58.710
Yeah. Well, he's always 
played to his own fiddle.

00:03:58.710 --> 00:04:00.260
I see.

00:04:00.690 --> 00:04:03.260
What's with the interest in Kai?

00:04:03.260 --> 00:04:08.290
Yes. I want to have a Vanguard 
Fight with Kai once again.

00:04:09.300 --> 00:04:11.280
If you wanna fight so bad,

00:04:11.280 --> 00:04:15.440
then the greatest Vanguard Fighter ever, 
Katsumi Morikawa, will be your opponent!

00:04:15.440 --> 00:04:17.150
I can't believe this guy!

00:04:18.650 --> 00:04:21.490
Did you already forget you just lost?

00:04:21.490 --> 00:04:24.120
LM's gotta be LM, yo!

00:04:24.120 --> 00:04:25.990
What the hell is "LM" anyway?

00:04:26.370 --> 00:04:29.700
Lose-umi Morikawa's initials, duh!

00:04:30.680 --> 00:04:33.540
I told you, my name is Katsumi, you little...

00:04:35.070 --> 00:04:37.710
I <i>believe</i> I said to keep quiet.

00:04:42.300 --> 00:04:47.300
The Fearsome Soulblast

00:04:47.930 --> 00:04:51.680
Sheesh... It's your fault we got yelled at.

00:04:51.910 --> 00:04:54.100
Back at you, dude.

00:04:54.100 --> 00:04:56.290
Why'd Aichi and me get involved?

00:04:56.290 --> 00:04:58.010
You started it.

00:04:58.010 --> 00:04:59.580
Yeah, that's right!

00:05:00.250 --> 00:05:02.210
Anyway, we're heading that way.

00:05:02.210 --> 00:05:03.700
Right. Later.

00:05:03.700 --> 00:05:05.110
Later, Kamui the Great!

00:05:05.110 --> 00:05:06.740
See you tomorrow, yo!

00:05:06.740 --> 00:05:07.200
Sure!

00:05:09.150 --> 00:05:12.020
Looks like the three of us actually 
live in the same neighborhood.

00:05:12.020 --> 00:05:13.200
It seems that way, yes.

00:05:14.030 --> 00:05:17.780
If I live in the same neighborhood as my 
dear brother Aichi, then Miss Emi is also...

00:05:19.850 --> 00:05:21.210
H-Huh?

00:05:24.330 --> 00:05:27.970
Oh? His place is also this direction?

00:05:27.970 --> 00:05:30.220
What? You didn't know?

00:05:30.220 --> 00:05:34.730
Nope. It seems he moved back to a different 
place than he lived when he was little.

00:05:35.050 --> 00:05:38.600
He never talks about his 
home or family at all.

00:05:38.600 --> 00:05:40.770
Really?

00:05:41.070 --> 00:05:44.030
And he doesn't speak to anyone 
at school other than me.

00:05:44.240 --> 00:05:48.590
And even I have never seen him 
outside of school or Card Capital.

00:05:48.980 --> 00:05:50.500
Which means...

00:05:50.500 --> 00:05:54.870
Running into him here is like 
encountering a super-duper rare card!

00:05:54.870 --> 00:05:56.140
Something like that.

00:05:56.500 --> 00:06:00.100
He didn't used to be like this...

00:06:02.110 --> 00:06:03.650
Let's follow him!

00:06:03.650 --> 00:06:04.130
Huh?

00:06:04.130 --> 00:06:06.210
Aren't you curious?

00:06:06.210 --> 00:06:09.890
If he hides it so much, who knows 
what kind of place he lives at?

00:06:09.890 --> 00:06:10.860
But...

00:06:10.860 --> 00:06:13.070
Hehe... Sounds like fun!

00:06:13.070 --> 00:06:15.890
Okay! Gotta hurry or we'll lose sight of him!

00:06:15.890 --> 00:06:16.930
Yeah!

00:06:22.270 --> 00:06:24.320
Good. He hasn't noticed.

00:06:24.320 --> 00:06:26.170
We should really stop this...

00:06:26.170 --> 00:06:27.940
This isn't right.

00:06:27.940 --> 00:06:29.620
What are you saying?

00:06:29.620 --> 00:06:33.110
How can you call yourselves his friends 
if you don't even know where he lives?

00:06:33.110 --> 00:06:34.160
Well...

00:06:34.160 --> 00:06:34.830
Oh!

00:06:35.420 --> 00:06:36.790
He turned the corner!

00:06:36.790 --> 00:06:38.730
After him!

00:06:43.180 --> 00:06:44.570
Huh?

00:06:46.380 --> 00:06:47.610
He's gone...

00:06:47.610 --> 00:06:49.260
What is the meaning of this?

00:06:54.830 --> 00:06:56.230
Even you?

00:06:56.230 --> 00:06:58.270
Still playing detective, even 
though you're in high school?

00:06:58.670 --> 00:07:02.080
Well, it sounded like fun, so...

00:07:02.390 --> 00:07:03.700
I'm sorry, Kai!

00:07:05.420 --> 00:07:07.160
This is my fault.

00:07:07.160 --> 00:07:09.780
I was... curious.

00:07:10.300 --> 00:07:11.740
Curious?

00:07:12.290 --> 00:07:15.130
You don't seem like you used to.

00:07:15.500 --> 00:07:19.600
And since I heard you won't tell Miwa 
anything either, I thought maybe something had...

00:07:19.600 --> 00:07:20.880
Stay out of my business.

00:07:22.520 --> 00:07:24.730
If I want to tell you something, 
I will tell you myself.

00:07:26.250 --> 00:07:27.320
Then...

00:07:28.470 --> 00:07:30.610
Will you tell me if I beat you?

00:07:30.610 --> 00:07:31.730
What did you say?

00:07:32.230 --> 00:07:36.290
If I beat you in a Vanguard 
Fight, will you tell me?

00:07:36.290 --> 00:07:37.470
As a friend...

00:07:37.780 --> 00:07:39.300
Don't make me laugh.

00:07:39.300 --> 00:07:42.310
It's pointless for me 
to fight you as you are.

00:07:43.560 --> 00:07:46.270
Listen carefully. I'll say it again.

00:07:46.270 --> 00:07:47.750
Stay out of my business.

00:07:48.830 --> 00:07:51.330
Whoa, there! Hold it, buddy!

00:07:51.630 --> 00:07:54.410
Why, you little chimp!

00:07:57.160 --> 00:07:59.240
Um, I think he meant...

00:07:59.240 --> 00:08:00.410
"Little Chump".

00:08:00.410 --> 00:08:01.740
Uki!

00:08:01.740 --> 00:08:03.680
Either way!

00:08:03.680 --> 00:08:05.670
Toshiki Kai, fight me!

00:08:08.330 --> 00:08:10.660
I hope you'll entertain me a little,

00:08:10.660 --> 00:08:11.880
Kamui Katsuragi.

00:08:22.850 --> 00:08:24.540
What's about to start?

00:08:24.540 --> 00:08:27.540
Kai and Kamui are going to 
fight, by the looks of it.

00:08:27.540 --> 00:08:31.670
Now that you mention it, it's the first 
time I've seen the two of them...

00:08:31.670 --> 00:08:36.070
It's a Vanguard fight between two 
renowned cardfighters who come to my store!

00:08:36.070 --> 00:08:37.940
I can't wait!

00:08:37.940 --> 00:08:39.530
Watch the register, 'kay?

00:08:41.760 --> 00:08:43.160
Even you, sub-manager?

00:08:46.110 --> 00:08:48.670
But I wanna watch too!

00:08:48.950 --> 00:08:51.600
Stand up <i>the</i> Vanguard!

00:08:51.600 --> 00:08:53.430
Lizard Runner Undeux!

00:08:54.530 --> 00:08:56.930
Adding in "the"? You think 
that makes you sound cool?

00:08:56.930 --> 00:08:59.390
Battlerizer!

00:09:03.620 --> 00:09:05.640
I don't like going first,

00:09:05.640 --> 00:09:07.410
but here I go. Draw!

00:09:07.410 --> 00:09:10.860
The Great Kamui rides the Screamin' 
and Dancin' Announcer, Shout!

00:09:11.810 --> 00:09:13.890
Shout is in da house!

00:09:13.890 --> 00:09:17.780
I use Battlerizer's ability and 
move him to the rear-circle.

00:09:20.660 --> 00:09:23.320
I can't attack this turn anyways,

00:09:23.320 --> 00:09:26.910
so I'll fish for a grade 
2 I haven't drawn yet.

00:09:27.640 --> 00:09:29.650
I activate Shout's skill!

00:09:29.650 --> 00:09:33.130
I drop a card from my hand, 
and draw one from the deck!

00:09:34.440 --> 00:09:35.940
Grade 1, huh?

00:09:35.940 --> 00:09:38.160
Ah, well. I call Shout!

00:09:38.650 --> 00:09:41.100
Once again, I swap out a card.

00:09:43.330 --> 00:09:45.590
Okay! I end my turn.

00:09:46.120 --> 00:09:48.840
And with that, your forces 
are all prepared, I see...

00:09:49.260 --> 00:09:52.970
But I have no intention of 
this cardfight lasting long.

00:09:52.970 --> 00:09:55.300
I ride the Embodiment of Armor, Bahr!

00:09:59.110 --> 00:10:01.740
And I call another Bahr.

00:10:02.190 --> 00:10:05.240
I attack my opponent's Vanguard 
with each Bahr!

00:10:09.420 --> 00:10:10.920
I don't defend.

00:10:12.770 --> 00:10:14.110
Damage check!

00:10:15.710 --> 00:10:16.800
Next.

00:10:18.380 --> 00:10:20.160
Check for a drive trigger.

00:10:23.390 --> 00:10:24.850
Damage check.

00:10:25.960 --> 00:10:27.600
My turn is over.

00:10:27.870 --> 00:10:29.550
It's my turn!

00:10:29.550 --> 00:10:32.140
The Great Kamui rides Genocide Jack!

00:10:36.690 --> 00:10:39.080
I call Tough Boy and Battlerizer!

00:10:41.210 --> 00:10:45.660
Counter Blast activated! I rev 
Genocide Jack into high gear!

00:10:45.660 --> 00:10:46.410
Oh?

00:10:46.840 --> 00:10:49.230
Finally, it's my turn to attack!

00:10:49.230 --> 00:10:50.830
The wait was killing me!

00:10:50.830 --> 00:10:54.340
First I attack the Vanguard, 
Bahr, with Tough Boy!

00:10:54.340 --> 00:10:55.990
Go Kamui, Go Kamui!

00:10:55.990 --> 00:10:57.710
GK, GK, yo!

00:10:57.710 --> 00:10:59.510
Check for a damage trigger...

00:11:00.130 --> 00:11:02.720
I support Genocide Jack with Battlerizer.

00:11:03.270 --> 00:11:07.680
Plus, thanks to it being a Nova Grappler, 
Battlerizer's power is +5000!

00:11:07.910 --> 00:11:11.160
And there's more! I activate 
Battlerizer's skill.

00:11:11.160 --> 00:11:15.190
In exchange for returning it to the deck 
at the end of this turn, it gains +3000!

00:11:15.430 --> 00:11:19.740
Which means... 3000 plus 5000 plus 3000 is...

00:11:19.740 --> 00:11:23.430
With a total of 22000, 
I attack your Vanguard!

00:11:30.100 --> 00:11:31.670
Check for a damage trigger...

00:11:32.400 --> 00:11:33.670
Trigger activated.

00:11:33.670 --> 00:11:35.860
I add +5000 to my Vanguard.

00:11:35.860 --> 00:11:37.470
And I draw a card as well.

00:11:37.470 --> 00:11:38.890
We're not done yet!

00:11:38.890 --> 00:11:43.470
With Shout's support, I attack your 
rear-guard Bahr with Battlerizer!

00:11:43.470 --> 00:11:46.120
I guard with Lizard Soldier, Ganlu.

00:11:51.030 --> 00:11:53.410
Tch. My turn's over.

00:11:53.410 --> 00:11:55.060
Battlerizer returns to my deck.

00:11:56.770 --> 00:11:58.320
Well, fine.

00:11:58.320 --> 00:12:00.780
I've dealt 2 damage to you.

00:12:01.040 --> 00:12:02.650
You aren't that bad.

00:12:03.130 --> 00:12:05.150
But that's as far as you get.

00:12:05.150 --> 00:12:07.450
I ride the Dragon Knight, Aleph.

00:12:10.370 --> 00:12:13.010
And I call the Embodiment of the Spear, Tahr.

00:12:14.660 --> 00:12:16.570
I activate Aleph's skill.

00:12:16.570 --> 00:12:19.840
By moving Bahr and Tahr 
to the Vanguard's Soul,

00:12:20.040 --> 00:12:23.700
I summon the Embodiment of 
Victory, Aleph, from my deck!

00:12:25.720 --> 00:12:28.350
Superior Ride the Vanguard!

00:12:28.750 --> 00:12:30.850
The Embodiment of Victory, Aleph!

00:12:31.420 --> 00:12:33.440
Grade 3, just like that?

00:12:34.070 --> 00:12:39.550
When it comes to Vanguard Fights, nothing is 
more important than who rides to grade 3 first.

00:12:39.550 --> 00:12:41.440
I think you realize this.

00:12:43.140 --> 00:12:46.530
Wow... Grade 3 and only the fourth turn?

00:12:46.530 --> 00:12:47.450
Not bad.

00:12:47.790 --> 00:12:50.660
The real fight starts now!

00:13:01.590 --> 00:13:03.350
I call the Flame of Hope, Aermo,

00:13:03.350 --> 00:13:05.250
the Dragon Knight, Nehalem,

00:13:05.250 --> 00:13:07.220
and the Wyvern Guard, Barri.

00:13:07.830 --> 00:13:09.980
I boost Aleph with Aermo,

00:13:09.980 --> 00:13:12.180
and attack Genocide Jack!

00:13:16.310 --> 00:13:18.240
Twin drive check.

00:13:22.930 --> 00:13:26.240
Dragon Monk, Genjo's drive trigger activated.

00:13:26.240 --> 00:13:28.530
Aleph's power is +5000!

00:13:28.880 --> 00:13:30.740
I also recover one damage.

00:13:35.610 --> 00:13:37.960
Also, because Aermo's boost was successful,

00:13:38.380 --> 00:13:40.450
I swap one card out from my hand.

00:13:41.140 --> 00:13:45.090
I boost Nehalem with Barri, 
and attack Genocide Jack!

00:13:48.430 --> 00:13:49.970
My turn is over.

00:13:50.730 --> 00:13:52.600
4 damage vs. 1...

00:13:52.600 --> 00:13:54.130
That's gettin' in the danger zone!

00:13:54.130 --> 00:13:55.990
Kamui's in the DZ, yo!

00:13:55.990 --> 00:13:57.610
I know, I know!

00:13:57.610 --> 00:14:00.190
Well, it's time for me 
to ride my own grade 3!

00:14:00.400 --> 00:14:04.190
The Super Great Kamui rides Mr. Invincible!

00:14:11.470 --> 00:14:13.810
Huh? Power of 10000 only?

00:14:13.810 --> 00:14:17.050
Genocide Jack's power is higher than that...

00:14:17.050 --> 00:14:19.460
Its grade is more important that its power.

00:14:19.710 --> 00:14:22.960
The most important thing is the twin drive.

00:14:23.180 --> 00:14:24.460
I see.

00:14:24.720 --> 00:14:27.140
First, Invincible's skill!

00:14:27.140 --> 00:14:32.100
I place one card from my deck in the Soul, 
and turn back over a card in my damage zone!

00:14:32.870 --> 00:14:33.850
Here I go!

00:14:34.520 --> 00:14:36.280
I call the King of Sword!

00:14:36.280 --> 00:14:38.070
Battlerizer, you're dismissed.

00:14:38.070 --> 00:14:42.490
I move Tough Boy to the back row, 
and call another King of Sword!

00:14:44.630 --> 00:14:48.490
I support the King of Sword with 
Tough Boy, and attack Aleph!

00:14:50.640 --> 00:14:52.570
I'll let that attack pass.

00:14:55.940 --> 00:14:58.890
I attack Aleph with Invincible!

00:15:02.860 --> 00:15:04.620
Twin Drive check.

00:15:06.050 --> 00:15:07.580
And the second check...

00:15:08.500 --> 00:15:10.850
All right, a critical trigger!

00:15:10.850 --> 00:15:14.970
I add +5000 to the power of the King 
of Swords that hasn't yet attacked!

00:15:14.970 --> 00:15:17.800
And Invincible's damage is +1!

00:15:21.550 --> 00:15:23.530
Check for a damage trigger...

00:15:23.530 --> 00:15:25.440
Critical trigger.

00:15:25.440 --> 00:15:27.500
I give all effects to Aleph.

00:15:28.860 --> 00:15:29.940
Check.

00:15:29.940 --> 00:15:33.810
I support the King of Sword 
with Shout and attack Aleph!

00:15:36.390 --> 00:15:37.660
I guard with Genjo.

00:15:37.920 --> 00:15:42.570
Um... Power is +5000, and 
Genjo's shield is 10000...

00:15:42.570 --> 00:15:45.080
At 25000, the attack won't go through!

00:15:45.760 --> 00:15:46.980
Dang...

00:15:46.980 --> 00:15:49.090
Tahr's trigger is in effect...

00:15:49.750 --> 00:15:52.600
But at least we both have 4 damage.

00:15:52.600 --> 00:15:53.550
I've caught up.

00:15:53.550 --> 00:15:55.240
Kamui the Great indeed!

00:15:55.240 --> 00:15:57.100
SS, yo!

00:15:57.100 --> 00:15:59.090
It's far too early to celebrate.

00:15:59.930 --> 00:16:02.270
Ride the Vanguard!

00:16:04.600 --> 00:16:06.550
Vortex Dragon!

00:16:12.840 --> 00:16:14.660
Look who shows up...

00:16:15.020 --> 00:16:16.910
Vortex Dragon?

00:16:16.910 --> 00:16:20.370
But if he uses that correctly, 
the kid'll be crushed...

00:16:20.570 --> 00:16:23.100
I place a card from the deck in the Soul.

00:16:23.100 --> 00:16:26.080
Vortex's power is +2000.

00:16:27.950 --> 00:16:29.550
I boost with Barri,

00:16:29.550 --> 00:16:32.110
and attack Invincible with Nehalem.

00:16:32.830 --> 00:16:34.840
I defend with the Ring Girl, Clara!

00:16:41.840 --> 00:16:42.850
In that case,

00:16:42.850 --> 00:16:47.540
I support with Aermo, and attack Invincible 
with the Vortex Dragon as well.

00:16:52.330 --> 00:16:54.390
What's wrong with Kamui?

00:16:54.390 --> 00:16:58.900
Kamui's already got 4 cards 
in his damage zone, right?

00:16:58.900 --> 00:17:01.790
In other words, 2 more damage and he's lost.

00:17:01.980 --> 00:17:07.990
Yeah. With the Twin Drive, just one 
critical trigger and it's over.

00:17:08.660 --> 00:17:10.380
He should defend against this one.

00:17:10.590 --> 00:17:12.950
But take a good look at Kamui's hand.

00:17:13.660 --> 00:17:15.450
He only has two cards, yeah...

00:17:15.850 --> 00:17:18.110
Taking into consideration the rest of the fight,

00:17:18.110 --> 00:17:20.640
you wouldn't want to deplete 
your hand any more...

00:17:21.010 --> 00:17:22.480
Kamui...

00:17:23.770 --> 00:17:24.900
I've decided!

00:17:24.900 --> 00:17:26.980
I intercept with the King of Sword!

00:17:26.980 --> 00:17:29.730
I also defend with the Shining Lady!

00:17:29.950 --> 00:17:31.410
Going to guard, are we?

00:17:31.410 --> 00:17:32.680
Excellent.

00:17:32.680 --> 00:17:34.490
Check the drive trigger...

00:17:34.490 --> 00:17:35.450
First check.

00:17:35.670 --> 00:17:37.490
All right, no mark!

00:17:37.490 --> 00:17:38.870
Second check...

00:17:39.730 --> 00:17:41.740
Critical trigger activated.

00:17:42.140 --> 00:17:44.800
Phew! That was a close one.

00:17:44.800 --> 00:17:46.380
That was a fine decision you made.

00:17:46.380 --> 00:17:49.210
If you had been afraid to play from 
your hand, it would have been over.

00:17:49.460 --> 00:17:52.630
Yeah, you don't have to remind me, buddy!

00:17:53.700 --> 00:17:54.710
Draw!

00:17:55.350 --> 00:17:57.770
I activate Invincible's skill!

00:17:58.240 --> 00:18:00.140
I don't have any damage to turn over,

00:18:00.330 --> 00:18:02.040
but I'll soul charge!

00:18:03.300 --> 00:18:06.280
And then I call Genocide Jack!

00:18:06.280 --> 00:18:08.690
Counter Blast to rev him into high gear!

00:18:08.920 --> 00:18:12.940
I support with Shout, and attack 
Vortex with Genocide Jack!

00:18:15.900 --> 00:18:17.910
I'll accept that attack.

00:18:17.910 --> 00:18:19.530
Check for a damage trigger...

00:18:20.230 --> 00:18:24.410
I add +5000 to Vortex Dragon's 
power, and draw a card.

00:18:25.490 --> 00:18:27.390
Your fifth damage, huh?

00:18:27.390 --> 00:18:29.820
One more and I win!

00:18:29.820 --> 00:18:32.550
I attack Vortex with Invincible!

00:18:32.550 --> 00:18:36.680
But with that critical 
trigger, its power is 15000!

00:18:37.960 --> 00:18:41.470
If one of the twin drives 
is a trigger, then...

00:18:41.470 --> 00:18:44.710
I see. He only needs one damage to win, so...

00:18:44.710 --> 00:18:48.230
Even if the chances are low, his 
plan is to take that chance.

00:18:48.230 --> 00:18:51.020
But Kai would surely have anticipated that.

00:18:51.020 --> 00:18:52.960
I guard with Genjo.

00:18:52.960 --> 00:18:56.460
Now the attacking power is lowered by 10000.

00:18:56.460 --> 00:18:58.440
The attack won't go through.

00:18:58.440 --> 00:19:00.280
Check the twin drive!

00:19:03.640 --> 00:19:05.690
No trigger activated.

00:19:06.300 --> 00:19:07.620
I see.

00:19:07.620 --> 00:19:08.050
Huh?

00:19:08.050 --> 00:19:11.180
The best outcome is if the 
attack hits, of course,

00:19:11.180 --> 00:19:14.060
but even if it fails, it allows him 
to increase the size of his hand.

00:19:14.060 --> 00:19:16.090
So that's why he attacked...

00:19:16.400 --> 00:19:21.280
I attack Vortex Dragon with the King 
of Swords, supported by Tough Boy!

00:19:21.280 --> 00:19:22.730
I guard with Tahr.

00:19:24.710 --> 00:19:26.480
Kai managed to defend the whole turn!

00:19:26.480 --> 00:19:29.230
Wow! Both of them are amazing!

00:19:30.040 --> 00:19:31.840
And now we're even.

00:19:32.570 --> 00:19:33.510
Draw.

00:19:33.940 --> 00:19:36.550
I place a card from the deck in the Soul.

00:19:36.550 --> 00:19:39.030
Vortex's power is +2000.

00:19:39.030 --> 00:19:42.900
I call the Dragon Knight, Nehalem, 
and Wyvern Strike, Jarran.

00:19:45.470 --> 00:19:49.230
Gonna attack with Vortex 
and Aermo again, huh?

00:19:49.230 --> 00:19:51.050
Your prediction is incorrect.

00:19:51.050 --> 00:19:51.860
What?

00:19:51.860 --> 00:19:55.250
That Jarran was the eighth 
card placed in the Soul.

00:19:55.250 --> 00:19:56.120
Crap!

00:19:57.590 --> 00:19:59.230
What? What's happening?

00:19:59.230 --> 00:20:02.860
The eighth card activates the Soul Blast.

00:20:02.860 --> 00:20:05.340
Vortex's scorching breath,

00:20:05.590 --> 00:20:07.040
Burning Hell!

00:20:09.320 --> 00:20:10.770
Picture it in your mind.

00:20:11.100 --> 00:20:15.390
The form of a ominous dragon, 
shaking the surface of Cray!

00:20:16.460 --> 00:20:18.770
Holding within it the swirling 
flames of hell itself...

00:20:18.770 --> 00:20:21.350
Burning the entire world to nothing but ash!

00:20:21.350 --> 00:20:23.000
Vortex Dragon!

00:20:26.920 --> 00:20:29.370
I retire three of your rear-guard.

00:20:33.680 --> 00:20:35.490
Now, for the finale.

00:20:35.940 --> 00:20:38.300
I boost Nehalem with Barri,

00:20:38.300 --> 00:20:40.250
and attack Invincible!

00:20:40.250 --> 00:20:42.920
That's 16000 power total...

00:20:45.010 --> 00:20:47.340
I can't defend, no matter what I play!

00:20:47.340 --> 00:20:48.890
There's only one hope left...

00:20:49.210 --> 00:20:50.610
Damage check!

00:20:53.300 --> 00:20:55.350
Trigger... no!

00:20:55.700 --> 00:20:57.230
This is it.

00:20:57.230 --> 00:21:02.320
With the boost of Aermo, I attack 
Invincible with the Vortex Dragon!

00:21:07.000 --> 00:21:08.380
Damage check!

00:21:10.250 --> 00:21:11.450
I lost!

00:21:11.450 --> 00:21:12.750
Kamui...

00:21:16.740 --> 00:21:18.420
That's all?

00:21:18.420 --> 00:21:20.700
Wait! Fight me again!

00:21:20.700 --> 00:21:21.590
I refuse.

00:21:21.590 --> 00:21:22.340
What?

00:21:23.020 --> 00:21:25.320
I've measured your ability.

00:21:25.320 --> 00:21:27.310
I will gain nothing from fighting you.

00:21:30.030 --> 00:21:31.100
Kai!

00:21:31.550 --> 00:21:33.200
Aichi Sendou...

00:21:33.920 --> 00:21:36.320
I believe I said to stay out of my business.

00:21:36.320 --> 00:21:40.600
Yeah. But I won't ask you to talk 
about things you don't want to again!

00:21:40.600 --> 00:21:42.270
I won't follow you, either!

00:21:42.770 --> 00:21:45.340
Because as long as I come 
here, I will meet you again.

00:21:45.340 --> 00:21:47.320
And I'll be able to fight you one day.

00:21:47.590 --> 00:21:49.400
You have not the power.

00:21:49.400 --> 00:21:50.590
I know.

00:21:50.590 --> 00:21:55.040
Just as you say... I may not be
someone worthy of fighting you now.

00:21:55.040 --> 00:21:57.210
But, I'll become stronger!

00:21:57.210 --> 00:21:59.000
So, one day, I'm sure...

00:22:01.000 --> 00:22:02.380
Suit yourself.

00:22:02.580 --> 00:22:04.180
Come again!

00:22:05.010 --> 00:22:06.970
He should be more honest with himself.

00:22:06.970 --> 00:22:08.730
Seriously.

00:22:08.730 --> 00:22:12.020
He is quite the talented fighter, yes?

00:22:12.360 --> 00:22:14.170
I can't wait!

00:23:51.340 --> 00:23:53.430
Kai really is amazing.

00:23:53.430 --> 00:23:55.710
Damn it all! I lost, lost, lost!

00:23:55.710 --> 00:23:58.690
But you're in elementary school, 
and Kai is in high school.

00:23:58.690 --> 00:24:01.720
So what? It doesn't matter if your 
opponent is older or younger than you,

00:24:01.720 --> 00:24:04.710
losing really sucks! Don't 
you think so, my brother?

00:24:04.710 --> 00:24:07.180
Yes.  Although I enjoy losing as well.

00:24:07.180 --> 00:24:10.340
But the feeling of frustration is 
important motivation to get stronger.

00:24:10.340 --> 00:24:12.280
At the next Shop Tournament, 
I'm gonna get my rebound!

00:24:12.280 --> 00:24:14.320
I think you mean revenge.

00:24:14.320 --> 00:24:16.660
Next time: The King of 
Knights Enters the Fray!

00:24:16.660 --> 00:24:18.640
The picture in my mind invites me to victory!
